<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · sea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Strait of Gibraltar</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Strait of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gibraltar">Gibraltar</a> is the narrow channel between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> linking the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> and the Atlantic. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravid Empire</a> crossed it to intervene in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a>. Accounts of the Almoravid Empire note its importance for trade.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/strait-of-gibraltar.jpg" alt="Strait of Gibraltar" width="320" height="317" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NASA · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:STS059-238-074_Strait_of_Gibraltar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
